event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":2246,"item_id":"fc_07c68c52ae025661016adb2fdf16ec8191aa8690c79d2206c4","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"spec\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"lie-module-irreducibility\\\",\\\"full_target\\\":\\\"For every prime p, every field K of characteristic p, every integer lambda with 0 <= lambda < p, and every admissible lattice M in the complex irreducible highest-weight sl2-module V(lambda), prove that M tensor_Z K is irreducible as the scalar-extension Lie algebra L(K)-module.\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"M tensor_Z K is irreducible as an L(K)-module, meaning it is nonzero and each K-linear subspace invariant under x,y,h is either zero or the whole space.\\\",\\\"parameters\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"p\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"prime number\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"K\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"field\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"M\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"admissible lattice in V(lambda) over Z\\\"}],\\\"hypotheses\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"p is prime.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"source-context.md, original target\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"K is a field of characteristic p.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"source-context.md, original target\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"lambda is an integer and 0 <= lambda < p.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"Exercise 7 and source-context.md\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H004\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"V(lambda) is the complex irreducible highest-weight sl2-module of highest weight lambda, with generators x,y,h satisfying [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=-2y, [x,y]=h and a nonzero highest-weight vector v with xv=0 and hv=lambda v; it has dimension lambda+1. M is any free abelian subgroup of V(lambda) whose Z-basis is a C-basis and for which U_Z M is contained in M, where U_Z is generated by X_r=x^r/r! and Y_r=y^r/r! for integers r>=0.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"source-context.md, definitions and exercise context\\\"}],\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"logic\\\":{\\\"classical\\\":true,\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"modus_ponens\\\",\\\"implication_introduction\\\",\\\"negation_introduction\\\",\\\"contradiction_classical\\\",\\\"case_elimination\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\",\\\"exists_elimination\\\"],\\\"calculations\\\":[\\\"Finite matrix multiplication, divided-power formulas obtained by iteration of the sl2 relations, localization and reduction of free modules, and explicit elementary ideal calculations in Z_(p).\\\"],\\\"primitives\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"C\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"field\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The complex field containing the characteristic-zero representation V(lambda).\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"Z_(p)\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"ring\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The subring R={a/b in Q: a,b are integers and p does not divide b}.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"U_Z\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Z-algebra of operators\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The Z-algebra generated on V(lambda) by X_r=x^r/r! and Y_r=y^r/r! for integers r>=0.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"L(K)\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Lie algebra acting on M tensor_Z K\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The K-span of the induced actions of x,y,h, obtained by scalar extension of the Chevalley Z-form.\\\"}]},\\\"pins\\\":{\\\"lean_version\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"inputs/problem.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"inputs/source-context.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"inputs/completed-proof.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"inputs/prior-candidate.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"}]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"lie-module-irreducibility\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"p\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"K\\\",\\\"p\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"p\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H004\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"V(lambda)\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"h\\\",\\\"v\\\",\\\"U_Z\\\",\\\"M\\\",\\\"C\\\",\\\"Z\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"M\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"L(K)\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"h\\\"]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let R=Z_(p), n=lambda+1, and e_i=y^i v/i! for 0<=i<=lambda. Iterating the given relations gives X_r e_i=binom(lambda-i+r,r)e_(i-r) and Y_r e_i=binom(i+r,r)e_(i+r), with an out-of-range e interpreted as zero. Thus these operators have integral matrices. Put M_R=R tensor_Z M inside V(lambda). Admissibility implies the R-algebra generated by all X_r,Y_r preserves M_R.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"R\\\",\\\"n\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"e_i\\\",\\\"v\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"X_r\\\",\\\"Y_r\\\",\\\"M_R\\\",\\\"M\\\",\\\"U_Z\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"In the basis e_0,...,e_lambda let E_ab send e_b to e_a and the other basis vectors to zero. The displayed divided-power formulas give Y_lambda X_lambda=E_lambda,lambda; X_(lambda-i)E_lambda,lambda=E_i,lambda; and E_lambda,lambda Y_(lambda-j)=binom(lambda,j)E_lambda,j. Since lambda<p, every binom(lambda,j) is a unit of R. Consequently every E_i,j belongs to the R-algebra generated by the divided powers and preserves M_R.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e_i\\\",\\\"E_ab\\\",\\\"X_r\\\",\\\"Y_r\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"R\\\",\\\"M_R\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"For each i set J_i={c in C: c e_i is in M_R}. The image E_i,i(M_R)=J_i e_i is finitely generated over R because M_R is finite free and an image of a finite module. It is nonzero: M_R spans V(lambda) over C and E_i,i is a nonzero projection. Since E_i,j preserves M_R, applying it to c e_j proves J_j subset J_i; reversing i,j proves equality. Denote the common module by J. Coordinate projections prove M_R=direct_sum_(i=0)^lambda J e_i. Tensoring with Q=Frac(R) and using rank_R(M_R)=n gives n=n rank_R(J), hence J has rank one. J is torsion-free as a submodule of C. A Q-linear identification Q tensor_R J=Q realizes J as a nonzero finitely generated R-submodule of Q. Clear denominators to obtain a nonzero finitely generated ideal of R. Every nonzero q in Q is p^k u for an integer k and a unit u in R; among a finite set of nonzero ideal generators choose the least exponent k. Every generator is in p^k R and one is p^k times a unit, so the ideal is p^k R. Hence J is free of rank one. For a generator a of J, the vectors a e_i form an R-basis of M_R.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"R\\\",\\\"Q\\\",\\\"M_R\\\",\\\"J_i\\\",\\\"J\\\",\\\"E_i,j\\\",\\\"e_i\\\",\\\"C\\\",\\\"n\\\",\\\"p\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S004\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"On the basis a e_i the actions are x(ae_i)=(lambda-i+1)ae_(i-1), y(ae_i)=(i+1)ae_(i+1), and h(ae_i)=(lambda-2i)ae_i, with out-of-range terms zero. Reduction modulo p identifies M_R/pM_R with M tensor_Z F_p: a Z-basis of M gives the same reduced basis and reduced integral action matrices. Since K has characteristic p, extension of scalars from F_p to K identifies M tensor_Z K with the standard module over K on this basis, as an L(K)-module.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"a\\\",\\\"e_i\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"h\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"M_R\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"F_p\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"M\\\",\\\"L(K)\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S005\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"For each 0<=r<=lambda<p, r! is invertible modulo p, so X_r and Y_r are scalar multiples of x^r and y^r on the reduced module. The matrix-unit identities in S002 persist modulo p because binom(lambda,j) is nonzero modulo p. Thus any K-subspace W invariant under x and y is invariant under every E_i,j. If w=sum_i c_i e_i is nonzero in W, choose i with c_i nonzero. For every j, E_j,i w=c_i e_j, so e_j belongs to W. Hence W is the whole module. The dimension lambda+1 is positive, so the module is nonzero. This proves irreducibility, including lambda=0 and p=2.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"X_r\\\",\\\"Y_r\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"E_i,j\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"W\\\",\\\"e_i\\\"] ,\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[]}]}}\"}"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":2247,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_07c68c52ae025661016adb2fdf16ec8191aa8690c79d2206c4","call_id":"call_07fb501ec1b84f9aa62cee7eeb658929","name":"check_artifact","arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"spec\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"lie-module-irreducibility\\\",\\\"full_target\\\":\\\"For every prime p, every field K of characteristic p, every integer lambda with 0 <= lambda < p, and every admissible lattice M in the complex irreducible highest-weight sl2-module V(lambda), prove that M tensor_Z K is irreducible as the scalar-extension Lie algebra L(K)-module.\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"M tensor_Z K is irreducible as an L(K)-module, meaning it is nonzero and each K-linear subspace invariant under x,y,h is either zero or the whole space.\\\",\\\"parameters\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"p\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"prime number\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"K\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"field\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"M\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"admissible lattice in V(lambda) over Z\\\"}],\\\"hypotheses\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"p is prime.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"source-context.md, original target\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"K is a field of characteristic p.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"source-context.md, original target\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"lambda is an integer and 0 <= lambda < p.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"Exercise 7 and source-context.md\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H004\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"V(lambda) is the complex irreducible highest-weight sl2-module of highest weight lambda, with generators x,y,h satisfying [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=-2y, [x,y]=h and a nonzero highest-weight vector v with xv=0 and hv=lambda v; it has dimension lambda+1. M is any free abelian subgroup of V(lambda) whose Z-basis is a C-basis and for which U_Z M is contained in M, where U_Z is generated by X_r=x^r/r! and Y_r=y^r/r! for integers r>=0.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"source-context.md, definitions and exercise context\\\"}],\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"logic\\\":{\\\"classical\\\":true,\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"modus_ponens\\\",\\\"implication_introduction\\\",\\\"negation_introduction\\\",\\\"contradiction_classical\\\",\\\"case_elimination\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\",\\\"exists_elimination\\\"],\\\"calculations\\\":[\\\"Finite matrix multiplication, divided-power formulas obtained by iteration of the sl2 relations, localization and reduction of free modules, and explicit elementary ideal calculations in Z_(p).\\\"],\\\"primitives\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"C\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"field\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The complex field containing the characteristic-zero representation V(lambda).\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"Z_(p)\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"ring\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The subring R={a/b in Q: a,b are integers and p does not divide b}.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"U_Z\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Z-algebra of operators\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The Z-algebra generated on V(lambda) by X_r=x^r/r! and Y_r=y^r/r! for integers r>=0.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"L(K)\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Lie algebra acting on M tensor_Z K\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The K-span of the induced actions of x,y,h, obtained by scalar extension of the Chevalley Z-form.\\\"}]},\\\"pins\\\":{\\\"lean_version\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"inputs/problem.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"inputs/source-context.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"inputs/completed-proof.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"inputs/prior-candidate.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"}]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"lie-module-irreducibility\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"p\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"K\\\",\\\"p\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"p\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H004\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"V(lambda)\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"h\\\",\\\"v\\\",\\\"U_Z\\\",\\\"M\\\",\\\"C\\\",\\\"Z\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"M\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"L(K)\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"h\\\"]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let R=Z_(p), n=lambda+1, and e_i=y^i v/i! for 0<=i<=lambda. Iterating the given relations gives X_r e_i=binom(lambda-i+r,r)e_(i-r) and Y_r e_i=binom(i+r,r)e_(i+r), with an out-of-range e interpreted as zero. Thus these operators have integral matrices. Put M_R=R tensor_Z M inside V(lambda). Admissibility implies the R-algebra generated by all X_r,Y_r preserves M_R.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"R\\\",\\\"n\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"e_i\\\",\\\"v\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"X_r\\\",\\\"Y_r\\\",\\\"M_R\\\",\\\"M\\\",\\\"U_Z\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"In the basis e_0,...,e_lambda let E_ab send e_b to e_a and the other basis vectors to zero. The displayed divided-power formulas give Y_lambda X_lambda=E_lambda,lambda; X_(lambda-i)E_lambda,lambda=E_i,lambda; and E_lambda,lambda Y_(lambda-j)=binom(lambda,j)E_lambda,j. Since lambda<p, every binom(lambda,j) is a unit of R. Consequently every E_i,j belongs to the R-algebra generated by the divided powers and preserves M_R.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e_i\\\",\\\"E_ab\\\",\\\"X_r\\\",\\\"Y_r\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"R\\\",\\\"M_R\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"For each i set J_i={c in C: c e_i is in M_R}. The image E_i,i(M_R)=J_i e_i is finitely generated over R because M_R is finite free and an image of a finite module. It is nonzero: M_R spans V(lambda) over C and E_i,i is a nonzero projection. Since E_i,j preserves M_R, applying it to c e_j proves J_j subset J_i; reversing i,j proves equality. Denote the common module by J. Coordinate projections prove M_R=direct_sum_(i=0)^lambda J e_i. Tensoring with Q=Frac(R) and using rank_R(M_R)=n gives n=n rank_R(J), hence J has rank one. J is torsion-free as a submodule of C. A Q-linear identification Q tensor_R J=Q realizes J as a nonzero finitely generated R-submodule of Q. Clear denominators to obtain a nonzero finitely generated ideal of R. Every nonzero q in Q is p^k u for an integer k and a unit u in R; among a finite set of nonzero ideal generators choose the least exponent k. Every generator is in p^k R and one is p^k times a unit, so the ideal is p^k R. Hence J is free of rank one. For a generator a of J, the vectors a e_i form an R-basis of M_R.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"R\\\",\\\"Q\\\",\\\"M_R\\\",\\\"J_i\\\",\\\"J\\\",\\\"E_i,j\\\",\\\"e_i\\\",\\\"C\\\",\\\"n\\\",\\\"p\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S004\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"On the basis a e_i the actions are x(ae_i)=(lambda-i+1)ae_(i-1), y(ae_i)=(i+1)ae_(i+1), and h(ae_i)=(lambda-2i)ae_i, with out-of-range terms zero. Reduction modulo p identifies M_R/pM_R with M tensor_Z F_p: a Z-basis of M gives the same reduced basis and reduced integral action matrices. Since K has characteristic p, extension of scalars from F_p to K identifies M tensor_Z K with the standard module over K on this basis, as an L(K)-module.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"a\\\",\\\"e_i\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"h\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"M_R\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"F_p\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"M\\\",\\\"L(K)\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S005\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"For each 0<=r<=lambda<p, r! is invertible modulo p, so X_r and Y_r are scalar multiples of x^r and y^r on the reduced module. The matrix-unit identities in S002 persist modulo p because binom(lambda,j) is nonzero modulo p. Thus any K-subspace W invariant under x and y is invariant under every E_i,j. If w=sum_i c_i e_i is nonzero in W, choose i with c_i nonzero. For every j, E_j,i w=c_i e_j, so e_j belongs to W. Hence W is the whole module. The dimension lambda+1 is positive, so the module is nonzero. This proves irreducibility, including lambda=0 and p=2.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"X_r\\\",\\\"Y_r\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"E_i,j\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"W\\\",\\\"e_i\\\"] ,\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[]}]}}\"}","status":"completed"}}

